# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Coverage output (config is .coveragerc, which is tracked)
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Virtual environment
.venv/

# Runtime save file (per-machine progression)
save.json
save.json.*

# Asset cruft (OS metadata) and editor sources anywhere the game loads from --
# the game only loads PNGs, and a source file sitting beside a shipped strip is
# shipped to every player. The reserve's own sources are re-included below:
# an `.aseprite` we keep on purpose is version control's business, not cruft.
*.aseprite
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Effect-pack extras -- the game only loads the packed spritesheet.png. Matched
# at any depth so packs under assets/effects/weapons/<name>/ get the same rule.
assets/effects/**/preview.gif
assets/effects/**/sprites/

# Packaging outputs. Configs live in dist/<target>/ and are tracked; each
# target's generated output beside them is not. build/ is pygbag's hard-coded
# work/output folder (build/web, build/web-cache), copied into dist/web/out/.
build/
dist/desktop/out/
dist/desktop/out-console/
dist/desktop/work/
dist/web/out/

# The reserve art library: packs and spare sprites kept for reference, never
# loaded by the game (`ASSET_DIRS` in dist/desktop/DeathliteGame.spec ships only the
# folders the data names). Untracked since 2026-09-12 -- ~300 MB, most of it the
# 61,783-file effects Gigapack that now lives inside it. The pack is also named
# on its own, matched at any depth, so dragging it back out cannot un-ignore it.
#
# The editor sources under it are the exception, and are tracked. `CREDITS.md`
# promises the `.aseprite` that came with the imp is "archived ... rather than
# deleted"; ignoring it made that promise unkeepable -- the file lived in one
# working copy and in no clone or `git worktree`, and the test asserting it had
# to skip itself everywhere else. It is 52 KB, and it is the source for art we
# ship, so it belongs in history. The four lines below are order-sensitive:
#
#   1. exclude everything under the reserve,
#   2. re-include its *directories* so git can descend into them at all
#      (git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded),
#   3. re-include the editor sources, which also beats the blanket
#      `*.aseprite` above because a later pattern wins,
#   4. re-exclude the Gigapack *last*, so git prunes its 61,783 files at the
#      directory instead of walking them on every `git status`.
assets/unused/**
!assets/unused/**/
!assets/unused/**/*.aseprite
Super Pixel Effects Gigapack/

# Editors and merge leftovers
.vscode/
.idea/
*.orig
*.rej

# Claude Code session data (worktrees, preview config)
.claude/
